course: dictionary
lesson: 12759
title: Dwelling: a formal word for home
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dwelling is a place where people live. It is a more formal word for house, flat or home, and you will often find it in history books, geography books and official forms. «The family moved into a small dwelling by the river.» Here dwelling means the family's home.
explain: Dwelling can also be a verb. To dwell means to live somewhere. «Early people dwelled in caves.» That means they lived in caves. You will see the -ing form in «cave dwellings», which are homes made inside caves.
explain: Dwelling has a second meaning. «Don't keep dwelling on the mistake» means don't keep thinking about it for too long, especially when it makes you sad. The phrase «dwelling on» is about thoughts, not houses. Check the sentence: does it make sense to say "thinking about" in its place? If yes, this is the second meaning.
fact: A dwelling is a house, flat or other place where people live.
fact: «Dwelling» is a formal word, so it is often used in history, geography and official papers.
fact: «Dwelling on» something means thinking about it for too long, often something sad.
fact: «Stone Age dwellings» were simple homes built by early people.
fact: A good check is to swap in the word «home»: if the sentence still makes sense, dwelling means a place to live.
exercise: «The family moved into a small dwelling by the river.» What is a dwelling? | A kind of boat used on rivers | A long walk beside the water | *A place where people live | A type of river fish
exercise: «Don't keep dwelling on the mistake.» What does dwelling on mean here? | Forgetting it as quickly as possible | Laughing about it with friends | Drawing a picture of it | *Thinking about it for too long
exercise: «Cave dwellings were the first homes of many early people.» Find and copy one word that means homes. | early | *dwellings | people | cave
test: «The farmhouse was a cosy dwelling for five people.» Which everyday word could replace dwelling? | Garden | Forest | *Home | Road
test: Ella says, «Stop dwelling on the broken toy.» What is she asking Sam to do? | Put the toy in a dwelling | Buy a new toy from the shop | Go and fix the toy right now | *Stop thinking about it for so long
exam: «Stone Age people lived in simple ___ made of wood and mud.» Which word fits best? | *dwellings | trumpets | whistles | puddles
